<Base
  title="Journey — Kevin A. Shah"
  description="From Chemical Engineering at IIT Gandhinagar to founding-team AI engineer — a path chosen on purpose."
>
  <main class="container">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Journey</p>
      <h1>I chose this path on purpose.</h1>
      <p class="lead muted">
        I’m an AI engineer on the founding team of aiRA, Capillary’s agentic AI platform. I didn’t
        arrive here by default. I studied Chemical Engineering at IIT Gandhinagar — a non-circuit
        branch — routed myself toward AI deliberately, then walked into industry as a product analyst
        and taught myself into engineering, earning a promotion each year.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        I think of a career less as a sequence of jobs and more as the slow accumulation of
        engineering judgment. Most of what’s below was chosen, or grabbed, for what it would teach me.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="section-label">The path</p>
      <ul class="timeline">
        {
          timeline.map((t) => (
            <li class:list={[{ mark: t.mark }]}>
              <div class="period">{t.period}</div>
              <div class="t-title">{t.title}</div>
              <div class="t-org">{t.org}</div>
              <p class="t-note">{t.note}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="section-label">How I think about engineering</p>
      <ul class="principles">
        {
          principles.map((pr) => (
            <li>
              <h3>{pr.h}</h3>
              <p>{pr.p}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <a class="link" href="/philosophy">The fuller version — why I build →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="section-label">Beyond the work</p>
      <div class="beyond">
        <p>
          Outside engineering, I’m an athlete — or I keep insisting on being one. I played football
          through school and for IIT Gandhinagar’s inter-IIT team. I’ve since reconstructed the ACL in
          both knees, on different legs, about two years apart: the first in November 2023, the second
          — with a meniscus tear — in September 2025. Between the two surgeries I ran three
          half-marathons, including the Tuffman Bengaluru and the Apollo Delhi, and had started
          training for a full one. I’m back in rehab now, working a return-to-sport protocol toward
          playing again.
        </p>
        <p>
          Rehab has taught me more about patience and honest progress than almost anything else. You
          can’t rush a healing ligament and you can’t fake the milestones — and it’s not lost on me how
          much that resembles the engineering I care about: long games, compounding effort, and no
          shortcuts that don’t eventually cost you.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also sing Indian classical music and play the keyboard. It’s the part of the day that
          isn’t optimizing for anything, and I’d like to keep it that way.
        </p>
        <p class="figure-note">Photos from the pitch and the road — coming soon.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p>
        <a class="link" href="/work">See the work →</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
